---
name: sim-render-split
description: Why {{PROJECT_NAME}} keeps game logic engine-free, and what breaks when it does not
metadata:
  type: project
---

Game logic in {{PROJECT_NAME}} lives in `sim/` and knows nothing about Godot:
no `Node`, no scene tree, no `Input`, no `Time`, no unseeded RNG, no iteration
over an unordered `Dictionary` where order affects the result. Classes there
extend `RefCounted`.

**Why:** it is what makes the replay gate possible. Same seed plus same tick
count must produce the same state hash, and every one of the things listed above
introduces a source of variation the seed does not control. It also means the
whole simulation is testable headlessly, and that projection (top-down now,
possibly isometric later) is a rendering decision rather than a rewrite.

**How to apply:** if a change appears to need a `Node` inside `sim/`, that is the
signal the design put logic in the wrong layer. Raise it rather than reaching for
an exception — the first exception is the one that makes the gate meaningless,
and after that nobody trusts it.
